+## Queueing one launch behind another
+
+Two tasks that contend for one GPU, port, disk, or box must not run at the same time. `afterTaskId: "<id>"` holds this launch until that task reaches a terminal state; `queue: "<name>"` serializes it behind the previous member of that named queue. The call returns immediately with `status: "queued"`, a real task id, and the output path the task will use, so `bg_status`, `bg_logs`, `bg_kill`, and the dock all work on it before it spawns.
